// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Edge glow on floors and ceilings. Reverse ambient occlusion: AO darkens
// where surfaces meet, this brightens the same places.
//
// NOT the same thing as Glow in the Dark above, and the menu says so, because
// both make floors glow and confusing them wastes an evening. GITD paints a
// glow COLOUR onto a sector, which then rises up the surrounding WALLS -- the
// floor itself never changes. This lights the floor SURFACE, inward from its
// own edges. They stack; neither needs the other.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

